I look for a warm top instead.
Many sweaters and sweatshirts are lying on a table.
I see a thick, grey sweatshirt.
It looks very warm.
I search in the stack.
I find the sweatshirt in size M.
I take it and go to the fitting room.
The cubicle is free.
I go inside and close the door.
Then I put the grey sweatshirt on.
It fits very well, and it is extremely comfortable.
I like to wear grey clothes.
I look at the price tag.
The sweatshirt costs forty-five Euro.
That is not expensive, because the material is great.
I want to buy the sweatshirt.
So I take it off again.
I take the sweatshirt and the green coat over my arm.
